      <link>https://www.kpbs.org/news/2026/01/20/why-it-matters-hotel-tax-to-expand-convention-center-falls-short-of-expectations</link>
      <description>The money is finally coming in — six years after a majority of San Diego voters approved an increase to the hotel room tax. It was billed as a way to expand the Convention Center, fund road repair and support homeless services. But it doesn't look like a new Convention Center will be coming anytime soon.</description>
